    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0970" n="856" xml:id="pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/344: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winslow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-20T12:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received, September 20—5:52
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Embassy informed. Japanese evacuation zone 1 completed September 18th.
                    General Tachibana<anchor n="75" xml:id="d748-f1"/> declares that evacuation zone
                    2 begins today. It is now technically possible for Chita troops to enter
                    Nikolsk.</p>
                <p>Steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Tomsk</hi> left here yesterday for Okhotsk
                    carrying reenforcements for White General Pepelaieff<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d748-f2"/> now operating with outlaw Blokhareff there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winslow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d748-f1" n="75" xml:id="d748-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Koichiro Tachibana, in command of Japanese forces in Siberia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d748-f2" n="76" xml:id="d748-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Anatoli Nikolaevich Pepelyaev.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
